## Only printf is referenced (by the printf member), so the default
## --gc-sections removes the options member's __local_stdio_scanf_options,
## and the initializer applies bits only to the function the link keeps.
# RUN: %{opts} noinc.txt | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NOINC-OPTS
# NOINC-OPTS-NOT: __local_stdio_scanf_options
# NOINC-OPTS:     {{^}}options __local_stdio_printf_options |= 0x24{{$}}
# NOINC-OPTS-NOT: __local_stdio_scanf_options
## With --no-gc-sections the link keeps both definitions, and both get their
## bits.
